    <exercise number="64" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>For the special “low-carb”trail mix, there are 1,000 pieces of mix. The total number of carbohydrates is 425 g, and the total amount of fat is 570.2 g. If there are 200 more pieces of cashews than cranberries, how many of each item is in the trail mix?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="65" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>For the “hiking” mix, there are 1,000 pieces in the mix, containing 390.8 g of fat, and 165 g of protein. If there is the same amount of almonds as cashews, how many of each item is in the trail mix?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>300 almonds, 400 cranberries, 300 cashews</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="66" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>For the “energy-booster” mix, there are 1,000 pieces in the mix, containing 145 g of protein and 625 g of carbohydrates. If the number of almonds and cashews summed together is equivalent to the amount of cranberries, how many of each item is in the trail mix?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
